tebooks | Workbenches | Implementation | P0 |\n71\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E004 | First-pipeline tutorial | Data Science Pipelines | RHOAI Pipelines | Implementation | P0 |\n72\t| RHAISTRAT-9019-E005 | Tutorial gallery usage and contribution documentation | Documentation | RHOAI Documentation | Implementation (docs-authoring) | P1 |\n73\t\n74\t## Dependency DAG\n75\t\n76\t```mermaid\n77\tgraph TD\n78\t    E001[\"E001 Tutorial packaging format\"] --> E002[\"E002 Dashboard gallery + launch\"]\n79\t    E001 --> E003[\"E003 Notebook tutorial suite\"]\n80\t    E001 --> E004[\"E004 First-pipeline tutorial\"]\n81\t    E001 --> E005[\"E005 Gallery + contribution docs\"]\n82\t    E002 --> E005\n83\t    E003 --> E005\n84\t    E004 --> E005\n85\t```\n86\t\n87\t## DAG Justification\n88\t\n89\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n90\t|------|------|-----------|\n91\t| E001 → E002 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The gallery's code builds against the packaging format (metadata, pinned images) — an API/schema-like contract, not a configuration reference. |\n92\t| E001 → E003 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | Notebook tutorials are packaged and validated per the format. |\n93\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 13 (build-against artifact) | The pipeline tutorial is packaged and validated per the format. |\n94\t| E001, E002, E003, E004 → E005 | Rule 11 (docs last) | docs-authoring is blocked by every Implementation epic; the docs describe the gallery and contribution process as built. |\n95\t| E002 ∥ E003 ∥ E004 | Rules 14/15 (parallel) | After the format contract exists, gallery code and tutorial content share no build artifacts; they live in different repos/work products and run in parallel. End-to-end launch verification is an AC on the gallery epic using a format-conformant package, not a DAG edge. |\n96\t\n97\tShared-surface note (Step 5 boundary rule 1): HLR-3's packaging format is a\n98\t**contract producer** (a schema the gallery code and the tutorial content both\n99\tbuild against — Rule 13), not an enforcement-tool extraction. The per-tutorial\n100\tvalidation runs are divided per surface: each tutorial epic's Acceptance\n101\tCriteria require its own tutorials to pass their validation manifests against\n102\tthe current release. The format itself is defined exactly once (E001) so no two\n103\tepics build the same data structure independently.\n104\t\n105\tNo Investigation epics: the strategy's Open Questions section is \"None\", and the\n106\trisks/assumptions/conditional-ADR scan finds nothing else that would change\n107\twhich epics exist or what they do.\n108\t\n109\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n110\t\n111\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n112\t|-----|----------|---------|-------|\n113\t| HLR-1 | P0 | E002 | Dashboard gallery with one-click launch (workbench with notebook, or pipeline import). |\n114\t| HLR-2 | P0 | E003, E004 | Split at the component/team boundary (Step 5 rule 1): five notebook journeys (Notebooks/Workbenches) and the pipeline journey (Data Science Pipelines/RHOAI Pipelines) are different components with different owning teams and review cycles. Together they cover all six curated tutorials, each tested against the current release. |\n115\t| HLR-3 | P1 | E001 (inherits P0) | Not deferrable: the format is the shared contract both HLR-1 (gallery launch reads metadata and pinned images) and HLR-2 (tutorials packaged and validated per the format) build against, so E001 blocks all P0 work and is P0 by priority inheritance. The per-surface validation runs are ACs on E003/E004. |\n116\t| HLR-4 | P2 | E005 | docs-authoring epic. Priority via the docs-authoring exception (Step 4): strategy frontmatter priority Major → P1, exempt from priority inheritance. |\n117\t\n118\tFull coverage: HLR-1 through HLR-4 all map to at least one epic; no orphaned\n119\trequirements.\n120\t\n121\t## Health Warnings\n122\t\n123\t- **Missing strategy sections (non-blocking):** no Impacted Teams, Dependencies,\n124\t  Acceptance Criteria, NFRs, Technical Approach, or Staff Engineer Input.\n125\t  Teams were taken from architecture-context owning teams; the Documentation\n126\t  team (\"RHOAI Documentation\") is assumed — verify with the strategy author.\n127\t- **Priority label inversion in the strategy (non-blocking):** HLR-3 is labeled\n128\t  P1 yet is a hard prerequisite of all P0 work (HLR-1/HLR-2 build against the\n129\t  format). Resolved structurally via priority inheritance (E001 is P0); the\n130\t  strategy's P1 label appears to reflect authoring sequence, not deferrability.\n131\t- **Epic size over the ~2-week guideline (E003):** E003 authors and validates\n132\t  five tutorials — estimated at 1.5–2 sprints of content work, at or slightly\n133\t  above the guideline. Kept whole because all five are the same work-product\n134\t  type for one team with one content review cycle, and a split by tutorial\n135\t  count would fragment the single validation pass against the current release\n136\t  into multiple cycles without changing owners or review paths. Re-split\n137\t  trigger: if fewer than three tutorials are authored-and-validated by the end\n138\t  of the first sprint (i.e. remaining scope still exceeds a sprint), split the\n139\t  remaining tutorials into a follow-on content epic.\n140\t- **Tutorial-to-runtime assignment assumption:** \"first RAG app\" is assumed\n141\t  notebook-based (assigned to E003). If the content team authors it as a\n142\t  pipeline, it moves to the pipeline tutorial epic (E004). This is an\n143\t  implementation detail — it does not change which epics exist or their\n144\t  boundaries.\n145\t- **Documentation lacks an architecture-context file:** treated as a docs\n146\t  content work stream rather than a new component to onboard (no\n147\t  repo/konflux onboarding chain is generated); flagged here for signal-9\n148\t  scoring (E005 architecture_claims = 0).\n149\t\n150\t## Tiered Delivery\n151\t\n152\tNot applicable — no external dependencies with uncertain timing; all work is\n1