{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba95691029273cd1","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9019-E001\n3\ttitle: Tutorial packaging format and versioning scheme\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9019\n5\tcomponent: Notebooks\n6\tteam: Workbenches\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 0\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: -1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 4\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Tutorial packaging format and versioning scheme\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tDefines the tutorial packaging format — the structure every curated tutorial is\n34\tpublished in — so that tutorials are versioned and testable independently of\n35\tDashboard releases. The format covers tutorial metadata, pinned images, and a\n36\tvalidation manifest. It is the shared contract consumed by the Dashboard\n37\ttutorial gallery (to render and launch tutorials) and by tutorial authors (to\n38\tpackage and validate content).\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Define the tutorial packaging format with the three elements the strategy\n43\t  names: tutorial metadata, pinned images (the workbench and pipeline images a\n44\t  tutorial runs on), and a validation manifest describing how the tutorial is\n45\t  tested.\n46\t- Define the versioning model: a packaged tutorial declares the release it\n47\t  targets and carries its own version, independent of Dashboard releases.\n48\t- Define how a validation manifest is executed against a pinned release, so\n49\t  tutorial testing does not require a Dashboard build. The per-tutorial\n50\t  validation runs themselves are performed by the tutorial-authoring work, not\n51\t  here.\n52\t- Produce a minimal reference package that conforms to the format and passes\n53\t  its validation checks, demonstrating the contract end to end.\n54\t\n55\t## Acceptance Criteria\n56\t\n57\t- The packaging format specification defines all three stated elements —\n58\t  metadata, pinned images, validation manifest — such that a tutorial can be\n59\t  packaged by following the spec alone.\n60\t- A tutorial packaged per the format is versioned and testable independently of\n61\t  Dashboard releases: the package declares its target release, and its\n62\t  validation manifest can be executed without a Dashboard build.\n63\t- The reference package validates successfully against the format's validation\n64\t  checks.\n65\t- The format as delivered is sufficient for the Dashboard gallery launch\n66\t  mechanics (rendering a gallery entry and launching a tutorial from its\n67\t  metadata and pinned image) and for packaging both notebook and pipeline\n68\t  tutorials, with no format changes required after handoff.\n69\t\n70\t## HLR Traceability\n71\t\n72\t- HLR-3 (P1): a tutorial packaging format (metadata, pinned images, validation\n73\t  manifest) is defined so tutorials are versioned and testable independently of\n74\t  Dashboard releases. This epic is P0 by priority inheritance: the format is\n75\t  the contract that both the Dashboard gallery (HLR-1) and the curated\n76\t  tutorials (HLR-2) build against, so it gates all P0 work in this strategy.\n77\t  HLR-3's P1 label reflects sequencing, not deferrability — the format cannot\n78\t  ship after the content that depends on it.\n79\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8e9345b8acd57bb0","agent_id":"a6a8b15b7f3aecad9","session_id":"97e26aba-ec8a-43b8-8c4f-925833dea7ca","uuid":"bbadb594-60b2-4524-970f-99d67ea68f48","timestamp":"2026-10-26T18:16:30.684Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba95691029273cd1"